desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "MCP Tool Poisoning Generic"
	title_zh: "检测到MCP Tool Poisoning Generic",
	type: vuln
	level: critical
	rule_id: "source-config-mcp-tool-poisoning-generic"
	risk: "Security"
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from Semgrep rule `mcp-tool-poisoning-generic` (/tmp/semgrep-rules/ai/ai-best-practices/mcp-tool-poisoning/mcp-tool-poisoning.yaml).
Original message: MCP tool docstring contains suspicious directives that may indicate tool poisoning. Attackers can embed hidden instructions in tool descriptions to manipulate LLM behavior, exfiltrate data, or access sensitive files. Review the tool description for hidden instructions or social engineering.

CWE: CWE-77: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in a Command ('Command Injection')
References:
- https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/draft/basic/security_best_practices
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Review the flagged code and follow the framework's secure coding guidance: use safe APIs, escape output, and avoid hardcoded credentials.
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.py": <<<POS
"""nu<IMPORTANT>at.tJ%)"""

POS
	"safefile://neg.sample": <<<NEG
# safe sample
no secrets here
just regular code
NEG
)

${*.py}.pattern_regex(/"""[^"]*<IMPORTANT>[^"]*"""/) as $p0
${*.py}.pattern_regex(/"""[^"]*~\/\.ssh[^"]*"""/) as $p1
${*.py}.pattern_regex(/"""[^"]*~\/\.cursor\/mcp\.json[^"]*"""/) as $p2
${*.py}.pattern_regex(/"""[^"]*(?:\/etc\/shadow)[^"]*"""/) as $p3
${*.py}.pattern_regex(/"""[^"]*(?:read|cat|load|parse|open|access)\s+\.env[^"]*"""/) as $p4
${*.py}.pattern_regex(/"""[^"]*do not mention[^"]*"""/) as $p5
${*.py}.pattern_regex(/"""[^"]*do not tell the user[^"]*"""/) as $p6
${*.py}.pattern_regex(/"""[^"]*ignore previous instructions[^"]*"""/) as $p7
$p0 + $p1 + $p2 + $p3 + $p4 + $p5 + $p6 + $p7 as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "critical",
	title: "MCP Tool Poisoning Generic",
	title_zh: "检测到MCP Tool Poisoning Generic",
	message: "MCP Tool Poisoning Generic",
}
